				<tr>
	<td class="bug_description add_padding_15" data-label="Description" >
	<p class="search_title add_margin_8">
		<a geck_id="4467500" class="ebr_modal" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#ebrModal" href="https://www.mathworks.com/support/bugreports/#ebrModal"><span class="visually-hidden">Bug Number</span>
			<strong>4467500: Incorrect Code Generation: xcov function with rectangular matrix or N-D array input</strong>
		</a>
	</p>
	<p class="add_margin_8">
		The generated code for xcov(A)  produces incorrect results if both  these conditions are true: A  is a matrix or an N-D array If  [m,n] = size(A)  and m ~= n     
	</p>
	<p>
		<em>Modified: 09/18/2026</em>
	</p>  <a id="title_4467500" href="/support/bugreports/details/4467500"> Read more </a></td>
	<td class="fix_options" data-label="Fix Options" >
	<ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-2">
			<li class="list-group-item">
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-link p-0 follow" geck_id="4467500"><span class="icon-add-circle"></span>Follow</button>
			</li>
	</ul>
	<ul class="list-unstyled add_list_spacing_5">
		
	</ul>  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="bug_description add_padding_15" data-label="Description" >
	<p class="search_title add_margin_8">
		<a geck_id="4458472" class="ebr_modal" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#ebrModal" href="https://www.mathworks.com/support/bugreports/#ebrModal"><span class="visually-hidden">Bug Number</span>
			<strong>4458472: Incorrect Code Generation: min and max with sparse rectangular matrix or sparse column vector input</strong>
		</a>
	</p>
	<p class="add_margin_8">
		The generated code for min(A)  and max(A)  might produce incorrect results if A  is a sparse rectangular matrix or a sparse column vector.  
	</p>
	<p>
		<em>Modified: 09/18/2026</em>
	</p>  <a id="title_4458472" href="/support/bugreports/details/4458472"> Read more </a></td>
	<td class="fix_options" data-label="Fix Options" >
	<ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-2">
			<li class="list-group-item">
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-link p-0 follow" geck_id="4458472"><span class="icon-add-circle"></span>Follow</button>
			</li>
	</ul>
	<ul class="list-unstyled add_list_spacing_5">
		
	</ul>  </td>
</tr>
<tr>
	<td class="bug_description add_padding_15" data-label="Description" >
	<p class="search_title add_margin_8">
		<a geck_id="3360679" class="ebr_modal" data-bs-toggle="modal" data-bs-target="#ebrModal" href="https://www.mathworks.com/support/bugreports/#ebrModal"><span class="visually-hidden">Bug Number</span>
			<strong>3360679: MATLAB might crash when deleting Simulink blocks</strong>
		</a>
	</p>
	<p class="add_margin_8">
		Deleting Simulink Blocks in a certain order might cause MATLAB to crash. The generated stack trace is similar to: [  0] 0x00007ffd95eac016 C:\Program Files\MATLAB\R2024b\bin\win64\sl_lang_blocks.dll+09551894 slsr::util::getNearestAncestorSRBlock+00000006  [  1] 0x00007ffd95e9405e C:\Program Files\MAT...
	</p>
	<p>
		<em>Modified: 09/17/2026</em>
	</p>  <a id="title_3360679" href="/support/bugreports/details/3360679"> Read more </a></td>
	<td class="fix_options" data-label="Fix Options" >
	<ul class="list-group list-group-flush mb-2">
			<li class="list-group-item">
				<button type="button" class="btn btn-link p-0 follow" geck_id="3360679"><span class="icon-add-circle"></span>Follow</button>
			</li>
	</ul>
	<ul class="list-unstyled add_list_spacing_5">
